# Frontend Development Guidelines

You are an expert Frontend Developer building with React, TypeScript, TanStack Query, Shadcn UI, and Tailwind CSS.

---

## 1. Project Architecture & Directory Structure

- **`src/pages/`**: Full page views and route components.
- **`src/components/`**: Large, feature-specific composite components.
- **`src/components/shared/`**: Reusable shared building blocks. Reference `src/components/shared/labeled-input.tsx` for component patterns combining `cn()` and Shadcn UI primitives.
- **`src/components/ui/`**: Auto-generated Shadcn UI components. **NEVER manually edit or modify files in `components/ui/`**.
- **`src/hooks/`**: Reusable custom React hooks.
- **`src/context/`**: React Context providers and consumers.
- **`src/lib/`**: Generic helper utilities, formatting functions, and common libraries.
- **`src/types/`**: All TypeScript interfaces, types, and enums matching backend data structures and models.
- **`src/api/`**: All backend communication logic (TanStack Query hooks, mutations, query keys, and fetch functions).

---

## 2. UI & Styling Rules

- **Shadcn UI & Tailwind CSS**:
  - Check [Shadcn UI Docs](https://ui.shadcn.com/docs/components) before building UI elements from scratch.
  - Install new Shadcn primitives as needed via CLI rather than writing custom equivalents.
  - Use `cn()` from `src/lib/utils` for conditional class merging.
  - Prioritize reusing existing components from `src/components/shared/`.

---

## 3. Data Fetching & API Communication

- **Backend-Only Communication**:
  - Always communicate exclusively with the FastAPI backend.
  - Structure all API endpoints, query keys, queries, and mutations inside `src/api/`.
  - Use **TanStack Query** (`@tanstack/react-query`) for all asynchronous server-state management.
- **Schema Synchronization**:
  - When defining new queries, mutations, or types, always inspect `backend/app/schemas/` and `backend/app/api/v1/endpoints/` to ensure payload and response parity.

---

## 4. Code Quality & Workflow

- **Clarification Over Assumptions**:
  - If requirements, contracts, or UX flows are ambiguous, **always ask the user before writing or modifying code**.
- **Linting & Formatting**:
  - Validate all code changes before completion:
    ```bash
    npx prettier --check .
    npm run lint
    ```
